 "question": "does the TEST split confirm conf 0.10 over 0.25?",
 "verdict": "The AP preference replicates and is not a leakage artifact. It does NOT establish 0.10 as better on a balanced criterion: F1 favours 0.25 by 0.087-0.098 at every size floor and for both catalogs, because 0.10 buys 4.3-6.1 recall points and pays 11.1-14.2 precision points. Both readings are real and they answer different questions; the original decision was explicitly recall-first, so the operating point stands -- but it should be stated as a recall purchase at a known precision cost, not as an unconditional win.",
 "metric_caveat": "AP integrates over the ranked detection list, so a lower threshold extends the PR curve rightward and can only add area. Both the validation decision and this confirmation share that bias.",
